  "configuration_id": "config_033",
  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 as RNA encoder dramatically outperforms scgpt (~0.72 vs ~0.52), and within the scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l family, transformer aggregation + weighted fusion is the best combo (0.725). The image encoder (imagenet_vit_l vs resnet50) is the major untested variable in this top-performing family. Question: Does resnet50 match or exceed imagenet_vit_l when paired with the best-known RNA encoder, aggregation, and fusion settings? Why this is the best next experiment: It directly extends the strongest evidence (scvi_n200 + transformer + weighted) by swapping only the image encoder, isolating that one design choice. With 3 experiments remaining, confirming or ruling out resnet50 as a superior image backbone is the highest-information test—if it helps, we gain a new best; if not, we lock in imagenet_vit_l and can spend remaining budget on profile setting (single vs multi) or other refinements."
}

